From 9e41421d5c65e805da6984538f0421c1745b3d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:09:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] qwen3_5: a looped checkpoint's plan and its
 manifold-constrained streams

SenseNova-Loop wraps the Qwen3.5 text tower with a shared-weight loop
and a two-stream mHC, both declared at the config's root. The shared
Spec now carries them: loop_plan.zig reads loop_settings and mhc as the
reference's execution_plan does (a fixed-count loop, a window inside
one loop phase, a learned Sinkhorn map), and answers the two questions
every backend asks: how many executions a forward runs (56 where the
checkpoint has 32 layers) and which physical layer each one visits.
The loader reads them after geometry, so the HIP path sees the same plan
the SenseNova recipe's CUDA series executes; a config without the
blocks keeps every layer once. model_type sensenova_loop is admitted
beside qwen3_5 and qwen3_5_moe.

Each visit of a looped layer needs its own cache slot; the engines that
have not caught up keep refusing looped checkpoints by the plan's own
rules until they do.
